<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helier de Carteret</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1532–1581</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helier de Carteret was a Jersey nobleman, Seigneur of Saint Ouen, who colonised the Channel Island of Sark. In 1565 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> granted him the island as a fief on condition that he keep it settled with at least forty men able to defend it against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> and the French. He divided Sark into forty holdings, laying the foundations of its feudal constitution, which lasted until 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helier-de-carteret.jpg" alt="Helier de Carteret" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrewrabbott · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memorial_to_Helier_de_Carteret_in_St_Peter%27s_Church,_Sark.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
